      {
        "id": 99956,
        "name": "Bas",
        "username": "Bas",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/b/a587f6/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2014-04-24T05:39:21.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"BrotherDusk\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/brotherdusk/48/2246_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> BrotherDusk:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>One thing I've been noticing is that there's a distinct lack of unnamed heroes being introduced in vengeance card art.&nbsp; It isn't like GTG to never hint ahead at new characters… the heroes I can think of that came with no hints or previous appearances before they dropped are:The Scholar, The Naturalist, Parse, and KNYFE.&nbsp;Correct me if I'm wrong, not claiming to be a card art expert here.EDIT: Personally, it makes me a bit sad that matching nemisis symbols is the endgame for determining what decks are coming in the future. It doesn't seem to me that perfect symmetry of baddies and their heroes is natural in a comic universe.&nbsp; There are always vestigial characters that go unused for years, are revamped, etc in comic lore.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>I think that Parse and KNYFE might be considered to have been PArtially hinted at in Miss Information's deck, on the card Insider Knowledge. But yes, they have had no appearance in person earlier on.</p>",
